# CCAT simulator tests

**References:** `projects/ccat-simulator/tests/sample-short.json`, `multiplication-678.json`  
**Validator:** `validateTest` in `projects/ccat-simulator/server.js`

## Where files live

- Path: `projects/ccat-simulator/tests/{slug}.json`
- `{slug}`: kebab-case English (e.g. `sample-short`, `multiplication-678`)
- Filename must match `^[a-zA-Z0-9._-]+\.json$` (server list/load safety)
- Prefer `id` equal to the filename without `.json`
- New files appear in the UI automatically after `npm start` — no code change

## Schema

```json
{
  "id": "my-drill",
  "title": "Human-readable title",
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q1",
      "area": "numerical",
      "stem": "Question text?",
      "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"],
      "answerIndex": 1
    }
  ]
}
```

| Field | Rules |
|-------|--------|
| `id`, `title` | Non-empty strings |
| `questions` | Non-empty array |
| `questions[].id` | Non-empty string; unique within the file (`q1`, `q2`, … is fine) |
| `questions[].area` | Exactly one of: `verbal`, `numerical`, `spatial`, `logic` |
| `questions[].stem` | Non-empty string (English) |
| `questions[].choices` | Array of ≥2 non-empty strings; prefer **4** choices (CCAT-like) |
| `questions[].answerIndex` | Integer index into `choices` (0-based); must point at the correct choice |

Malformed files are skipped in the test list or fail on load — always double-check `answerIndex` after writing choices.

## Content guidelines

- Persist **English only** (stems, choices, titles, filenames)
- Match the user's goal: full mixed mock vs skill drill (one area / one skill is fine)
- Keep stems short and scannable; no calculator-friendly multi-page setup
- Distractors should be plausible (adjacent table facts, off-by-one, common misreads) — not random junk
- Mix formats when useful: direct fact, missing term, short word problem, reverse operation
- Suggested length: ~8–12 for smoke samples; ~20–30 for focused drills; up to ~50 for full-length pacing practice
- Default pacing in the UI is ~18s/question (CCAT 15 min / 50); do not hardcode timing in the JSON

## Checklist before finishing

1. Every `answerIndex` matches the intended correct choice
2. No duplicate identical stems unless intentional review pairs
3. Areas tagged correctly for later attempt analytics
4. Spot-check a few products/logic answers by hand
5. Optional: load once via `GET /api/tests/{filename}` or start the simulator and select the new title

## Do not

- Put tests outside `projects/ccat-simulator/tests/`
- Change `server.js` / UI just to register a new JSON file
- Save Portuguese (or other non-English) into the JSON
- Add fields the validator/UI do not use unless the user asks to extend the schema
- Invent empty scaffolding or duplicate an existing drill under a new name
